<table style="width:100%">
  <tr>
    <td style="color:#223388; font-size:150%; vertical-align:middle"><span style="color:black; font-weight:600">NIST Atomic Spectra Database Lines Data</span><p>
      <u>Ne X</u>: 137 Lines of Data Found<br />
<span style="font-size:larger; font-weight:bold"><i>Z</i> = 10, H isoelectronic sequence</span><span style="font-size=300%">&nbsp;</span></p>
    </td>
    <td style="text-align:right; vertical-align:middle">
<div class='ref'>
<b>Example of how to reference these results:</b><br />

Kramida,&nbsp;A., Ralchenko,&nbsp;Yu., Reader,&nbsp;J., and NIST ASD Team (2024).
  <i>NIST Atomic Spectra Database</i> (ver.&nbsp;5.12),
  [Online]. Available: <span style="color:#0000cc;">https://physics.nist.gov/asd</span>
  [2025, March 22].
  National Institute of Standards and Technology, Gaithersburg, MD.
    DOI: <span style="color:#0000cc;">https://doi.org/10.18434/T4W30F</span>
<br />
<div style="text-align: right; font-size: x-small">
<a href="javascript:void(0)" onclick="popdef('/cgi-bin/ASD/bibtex.pl?y=2025&amp;m=March&amp;d=22');return true" target="_top">BibTex Citation</a> (new window)
</div>
</div>
    </td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td colspan="2">&nbsp;</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td colspan="2" style="color:#655665; font-family: helvetica,arial; font-size:80%"><b><u><i>&lambda;</i> in</u>: <span style="color:darkred">vacuum</span> <span style="color:navy"></span></b></td>
  </tr>
</table>

<p>
<table style="background-color:black; width:75%; border-spacing:1px" >
  <tr>
    <td colspan="3" style="color:white; font-size:10pt; width:70%; background-color:#224477; text-align:center">
      <b>Primary data sources</b>
    </td>
    <td rowspan="4">
    </td>
    <td style="white-space:nowrap; color:white; font-size:10pt; background-color:#446655; text-align:center">
      <table style="border:thin hidden;text-align:center;width:100%">
        <tr>
          <td style="text-align:center; white-space:nowrap">Query NIST Bibliographic Databases for</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td style="text-align:center"><b>Ne  X</b> (new window)</td>
        </tr>
      </table>
    </td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td class='brt1'>
      Energy Levels:
    </td>
    <td class='bcn'>
      &nbsp;<a onmouseover="self.status='Bibliographic Reference for Ne X';return true;" onmouseout="self.status='';return true;" target="_blank" href="javascript:void(0)" onclick="popded('https://physics.nist.gov/cgi-bin/ASBib1/get_ASBib_ref.cgi?db=el&amp;db_id=19200&amp;comment_code=&amp;element=Ne&amp;spectr_charge=10&amp;type=E');return false">Yerokhin&nbsp;&&nbsp;Shabaev&nbsp;2015</a>, <a onmouseover="self.status='Bibliographic Reference for Ne X';return true;" onmouseout="self.status='';return true;" target="_blank" href="javascript:void(0)" onclick="popded('https://physics.nist.gov/cgi-bin/ASBib1/get_ASBib_ref.cgi?db=el&amp;db_id=3620&amp;comment_code=&amp;element=Ne&amp;spectr_charge=10&amp;type=E');return false">Erickson&nbsp;1977</a>&nbsp;
    </td>
    <td class='blf'>
      &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;The data refer to the isotope <sup>20</sup>Ne. Erickson's theoretical values of ionization energies were scaled to the <a target="_blank" href="https://physics.nist.gov/constants">CODATA-2018 values of the fundamental constants</a> and then subtracted from the ground-state ionization energy given by <a onmouseover="self.status='Bibliographic Reference for Ne X';return true;" onmouseout="self.status='';return true;" target="_blank" href="javascript:void(0)" onclick="popded('https://physics.nist.gov/cgi-bin/ASBib1/get_ASBib_ref.cgi?db=el&amp;db_id=19200&amp;comment_code=&amp;element=Ne&amp;spectr_charge=10&amp;type=E');return false">Yerokhin&nbsp;&&nbsp;Shabaev&nbsp;2015 </a>. Additional corrections were applied to the <i>n</i>S levels, as described by <a onmouseover="self.status='Bibliographic Reference for Ne X';return true;" onmouseout="self.status='';return true;" target="_blank" href="javascript:void(0)" onclick="popded('https://physics.nist.gov/cgi-bin/ASBib1/get_ASBib_ref.cgi?db=el&amp;db_id=12548&amp;comment_code=&amp;element=Ne&amp;spectr_charge=10&amp;type=E');return false">Kramida&nbsp;et&nbsp;al.&nbsp;2008 </a>. The <i>n</i>&nbsp;=&nbsp;2 energy levels were taken directly from <a onmouseover="self.status='Bibliographic Reference for Ne X';return true;" onmouseout="self.status='';return true;" target="_blank" href="javascript:void(0)" onclick="popded('https://physics.nist.gov/cgi-bin/ASBib1/get_ASBib_ref.cgi?db=el&amp;db_id=19200&amp;comment_code=&amp;element=Ne&amp;spectr_charge=10&amp;type=E');return false">Yerokhin&nbsp;&&nbsp;Shabaev&nbsp;2015 </a>. Their uncertainties are given for excitation energies from the ground state; for the rest of the levels, uncertainties are given for separations from the ionization limit. The present data set was prepared by A. Kramida (unpublished) for the release of ASD v. 5.10 in September 2022.
    </td>
    <td class='bcn1'>
      <a href="javascript:void(0)" onclick="popbib('https://physics.nist.gov/cgi-bin/ASBib1/Elevbib/make_query.cgi?spectra=Ne%20X&amp;method=EL&amp;method=TE&amp;method=ND&amp;method=IP&amp;method=SF&amp;method=QF&amp;order=1');return false"
        onmouseover="self.status='Ne  X: bibliography energy levels query';return true;"
        onmouseout="self.status=''; return true;" target="_blank">Ne  X Energy Levels</a>
    </td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td class='brt1'>
      Lines:
    </td>
    <td class='bcn'>
      &nbsp;<a onmouseover="self.status='Bibliographic Reference for Ne X';return true;" onmouseout="self.status='';return true;" target="_blank" href="javascript:void(0)" onclick="popded('https://physics.nist.gov/cgi-bin/ASBib1/get_ASBib_ref.cgi?db=el&amp;db_id=19200&amp;comment_code=&amp;element=Ne&amp;spectr_charge=10&amp;type=L');return false">Yerokhin&nbsp;&&nbsp;Shabaev&nbsp;2015</a>, <a onmouseover="self.status='Bibliographic Reference for Ne X';return true;" onmouseout="self.status='';return true;" target="_blank" href="javascript:void(0)" onclick="popded('https://physics.nist.gov/cgi-bin/ASBib1/get_ASBib_ref.cgi?db=el&amp;db_id=3620&amp;comment_code=&amp;element=Ne&amp;spectr_charge=10&amp;type=L');return false">Erickson&nbsp;1977</a>&nbsp;
    </td>
    <td class='blf'>
      
    </td>
    <td class='bcn1'>
      <a href="javascript:void(0)" onclick="popbib('https://physics.nist.gov/cgi-bin/ASBib1/Elevbib/make_query.cgi?spectra=Ne%20X&amp;method=W&amp;method=CL&amp;order=1');return false"
        onmouseover="self.status='Ne  X: bibliography wavelengths query';return true;"
        onmouseout="self.status=''; return true;" target="_blank">Ne  X Line Wavelengths and Classification</a>
    </td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td class='brt1'>
      Transition Probabilities:
    </td>
    <td class='bcn'>
      &nbsp;<a onmouseover="self.status='Bibliographic Reference for Ne X';return true;" onmouseout="self.status='';return true;" target="_blank" href="javascript:void(0)" onclick="popded('https://physics.nist.gov/cgi-bin/ASBib1/get_ASBib_ref.cgi?db=tp&amp;db_id=7771&amp;comment_code=&amp;element=Ne&amp;spectr_charge=10&amp;type=T');return false">Jitrik&nbsp;&&nbsp;Bunge&nbsp;2004</a>&nbsp;
    </td>
    <td class='blf'>
      &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;The data of <a onmouseover="self.status='Bibliographic Reference for Ne X';return true;" onmouseout="self.status='';return true;" target="_blank" href="javascript:void(0)" onclick="popded('https://physics.nist.gov/cgi-bin/ASBib1/get_ASBib_ref.cgi?db=tp&amp;db_id=7771&amp;comment_code=&amp;element=Ne&amp;spectr_charge=10&amp;type=T');return false">Jitrik&nbsp;&&nbsp;Bunge&nbsp;2004 </a> have been scaled to the <a target="_blank" href="https://physics.nist.gov/constants">CODATA-2018 values of the fundamental constants</a> by A. Kramida for the release of ASD v. 5.10 in October 2022.
    </td>
    <td class='bcn1'>
      <a href="javascript:void(0)" onclick="popbib('https://physics.nist.gov/cgi-bin/ASBib1/Fvalbib/make_query.cgi?spectra=Ne%20X&amp;order=1');return false"
        onmouseover="self.status='Ne  X: bibliography transition probability query';return true;"
        onmouseout="self.status=''; return true;" target="_blank">Ne  X Transition Probabilities</a>
    </td>
  </tr>
</table>
    <p>
